<figure class="pgx-figure" data-spatial-figure aria-label="A square candidate is not a distance match">
 <figcaption><span>Figure 2</span> A square candidate is not a distance match</figcaption>
 <div class="pgx-scene pgx-spatial-layout">
  <svg viewBox="0 0 360 340" role="img" aria-label="A radius-five circle around the origin inside a square. A at 3,4 is on the circle. B at 4,4 is in the square but outside the circle. C at 6,0 is outside the square.">
   <rect class="pgx-box" x="35" y="35" width="250" height="250"/>
   <path class="pgx-rule" d="M10 160H335 M160 315V10"/>
   <circle data-distance-circle class="pgx-circle" cx="160" cy="160" r="125" hidden/>
   <path data-radius class="pgx-radius" d="M160 160L235 60" hidden/>
   <g class="pgx-svg-text"><text x="170" y="181">O (0,0)</text><text x="330" y="183">x</text><text x="174" y="16">y</text><text x="28" y="304">−5</text><text x="273" y="304">5</text><text x="4" y="43">5</text><text x="0" y="281">−5</text></g>
   <circle class="pgx-start" cx="160" cy="160" r="4"/>
   <circle class="pgx-point-a" cx="235" cy="60" r="6"/><circle class="pgx-point-b" cx="260" cy="60" r="6"/><circle class="pgx-point-c" cx="310" cy="160" r="6"/>
   <g class="pgx-svg-text"><text x="208" y="48">A</text><text x="267" y="48">B</text><text x="312" y="145">C</text></g>
  </svg>
  <div><p class="pgx-small">Separate mathematical points · coordinate units</p><dl class="pgx-point-list"><div><dt>A · (3,4)</dt><dd data-a data-live>Not tested</dd></div><div><dt>B · (4,4)</dt><dd data-b data-live>Not tested</dd></div><div><dt>C · (6,0)</dt><dd data-c data-live>Not tested</dd></div></dl></div>
 </div>
 <p class="pgx-step-explanation" data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">Find points at most 5 coordinate units from O. The square covers every possible match.</p>
 <div class="pgx-controls" role="group" aria-label="Figure 2 playback"><button data-play>Play</button><button data-back>Back</button><button data-next>Next</button><button data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 3</span><div data-hold><span></span></div></div>
 <p class="pgx-caption">A planar distance model. The square extends from −5 to 5 on each axis. It contains both A and B, but only A passes the distance test. This is not a PostGIS plan or a map of shop locations.</p>
 <details><summary>All stages, as text</summary><ol><li>Search within distance 5 of the origin in a Cartesian plane.</li><li>The enclosing square admits A (3,4) and B (4,4); it excludes C (6,0).</li><li>A has distance 5 and passes. B has distance √32, about 5.66, and fails. C has distance 6 and cannot pass. A bounding-box match is only a candidate.</li></ol></details>
</figure>
<script>
import {stepper} from '../figures/stepper.mjs';
for(const root of document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-spatial-figure]'))stepper(root,{steps:()=>3,draw:(step:number)=>{
 root.querySelector('[data-distance-circle]')!.toggleAttribute('hidden',step<2);root.querySelector('[data-radius]')!.toggleAttribute('hidden',step<2);
 root.querySelector('[data-a]')!.textContent=['Not tested','In box · candidate','Distance 5 · match'][step];root.querySelector('[data-b]')!.textContent=['Not tested','In box · candidate','Distance √32 ≈ 5.66 · rejected'][step];root.querySelector('[data-c]')!.textContent=['Not tested','Outside box · excluded','Distance 6 · already excluded'][step];
 root.querySelector('[data-explanation]')!.textContent=['Find points at most 5 coordinate units from O. The square covers every possible match.','The box can discard C. It cannot distinguish A from B: both coordinates lie between −5 and 5.','The distance test keeps A, including the boundary at 5. B was a useful candidate to test, but is not a result.'][step];
}});
</script>
